From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Jones <bajones@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:08:37 -0700
Subject: GL: Avoid FBO driver hash collisions

In some circumstances framebuffer objects with different attachment
layouts or where some draw buffers have been disabled, end up with
conflicting hashes in the PowerVR driver, causing internal state to not
update properly.

This change addresses both causes of the hash collisions by rebuilding
the native framebuffer whenever a potentially collision-producing change
is made. This prevents a cached hash from being used.

Bug: chromium:551065275
Change-Id: Ib82f3f3147d85175f6da028bae0858efe804cbce
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8551737
Commit-Queue: Brandon Jones <bajones@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Kenneth Russell <kbr@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): renderergl_utils.cpp on this branch has no isPowerVR local (the other PowerVR feature conditions call IsPowerVR(vendor) directly), so the new recreateFboOnAttachmentRespecification condition uses IsPowerVR(vendor); the FeaturesGL_autogen.h / gl_features.json entries are appended after this branch's finishBeforeSameTextureCopy. Everything else applies as upstream.

